title: Proposition 17
---
order: 17
---
short_label: XI.17
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If two straight lines are cut by parallel planes, then they are cut in the same ratios.
----
proof:

Let the two straight lines {AB} and {CD} be cut by the parallel planes {GH|GHT}, {KL|KLT}, and {MN|MNT} at the points {A}, {E}, and {B}, and at the points {C}, {F}, and {D}, respectively.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="310" height="320" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="XI.17 diagram" src="propXI17.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's figure: the parallel planes GH, KL, MN in oblique view, the
    // lines AB and CD cutting them at A, E, B and C, F, D, and the joins
    // AC, BD, AD, EO, FO, with O where AD meets the plane KL.
    //
    // Added, all transparent: GHT, KLT, MNT, faceless twins of the filled
    // planes (raised over the figure if highlighted, #140); the cutting
    // planes EBDO and AOFC; the triangles ABD and ADC; and the segments
    // AE, EB, CF, FD, AO, OD the ratios name. The joins are Joyce's own
    // lines, declared from the end they are drawn from.
